CM_ BO_ 2 "Steering angle sensor. Our testing confirmed steering-angle behavior, steering-rate behavior, fixed 0x07 field, approximately 100 Hz transmission, and 4-bit rolling counter.";

CM_ SG_ 2 STEER_ANGLE "Tracks physical steering-wheel position. Known Nissan scaling is 0.1 degree/count.";

CM_ SG_ 2 STEER_ANGLE_RATE "Tracks steering movement rate. Slow movement produces smaller values, fast movement produces larger values, and held steering returns near zero.";

CM_ SG_ 2 COUNTER "Confirmed 4-bit rolling counter. Sequence 0 through 15 then wraps to 0.";

CM_ BO_ 361 "Known Nissan LKAS steering-control message. Our capture confirmed approximately 100 Hz transmission, fixed 0x80 fields, 4-bit rolling counter, and CRC-8/SAE-J1850 checksum. DESIRED_ANGLE, MAX_TORQUE, and LKA_ACTIVE are established Nissan definitions and were not independently proven by the stationary test.";

CM_ SG_ 361 COUNTER "Confirmed 4-bit rolling counter. Sequence 0 through 15 then wraps to 0.";

CM_ SG_ 361 CHECKSUM "Confirmed CRC-8/SAE-J1850 over data bytes 1 through 7. Polynomial 0x1D, initial value 0xFF, final XOR 0xFF. Checksum stored in byte 8.";

CM_ BO_ 389 "Steering torque sensor. Our testing supports separate driver-torque and steering-angle behavior. Exact Nm and degree scaling follows the established Nissan definition.";

CM_ SG_ 389 COUNTER "Confirmed 4-bit rolling counter. Sequence 0 through 15 then wraps to 0.";

CM_ SG_ 389 CHECKSUM "Confirmed CRC-8/SAE-J1850 over data bytes 1 through 7. Polynomial 0x1D, initial value 0xFF, final XOR 0xFF. Checksum stored in byte 8.";

CM_ BO_ 634 "Observed turn-signal state message. Byte 4 bit 0 = left, byte 4 bit 1 = right. Both active = hazard. Message observed at approximately 50 Hz and stops when vehicle is off.";

CM_ SG_ 634 COUNTER_27A "Confirmed 4-bit rolling counter in byte 6 low nibble. Sequence 0 through 15 then wraps to 0.";

CM_ SG_ 634 CHECKSUM_27A "Confirmed additive checksum. Checksum = (Byte1 + Byte2 + Byte3 + Byte4 + Byte5 + Byte6 + 0x7C) & 0xFF.";

CM_ BO_ 943 "Observed hazard-switch press message. Byte 1 bit 7 pulses when the physical hazard button is pressed. Same pulse occurs for hazard ON and hazard OFF.";

CM_ BO_ 1549 "Door-status message also contains turn-signal state. Byte 2 bit 5 = left, byte 2 bit 6 = right. Both active = hazard. No obvious rolling counter or checksum observed.";
